      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://bigsurkate.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/IMG_3289-rotated.jpeg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://bigsurkate.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/IMG_3289-rotated.jpeg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<p>Last night was wild. Got about 2 hrs of sleep from 6:30 to 8:30, once the flames around the property subsided. Calfire operated a burn from Plaskett ridge road above our water tanks down to the highway and kept it to the south side of our house and Merritts. As far as I’ve heard, no structures &#8230; <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://bigsurkate.blog/2026/08/29/lower-plaskett-fire-photos-by-sarah-harvey/\">Continue reading <span class=\"screen-reader-text\">Lower Plaskett Fire Photos by Sarah Harvey</span></a></p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://bigsurkate.blog/2026/08/29/lower-plaskett-fire-photos-by-sarah-harvey/\">Lower Plaskett Fire Photos by Sarah Harvey</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://bigsurkate.blog\">BigSurKate</a>.</p>",
